  "Read from 200 dpi greyscale crops, one system at a time, enlarged 1.3x; Busoni uses two and three staves, so marks were assigned to voices by pitch and the note list.",
  "Economical pass: fingerings, \"M.D./l.H./r.H.\" hand signs, the parenthesised octave \"(voll)\" in the coda bass and the final-bar ossia are not transcribed; Busoni's many long slurs were taken only where they shape a line (phrase slurs on the running eighths), and are mostly marked likely.",
  "The final fermatas stand over all five voices; only the alto and tenor have a note starting in bar 115, so the fermatas are attached to those two (the others hold notes begun in bars 112 and 114).",
